      "html": "<p>Pseudochalceus kyburzi usually attains a length of about 5 cm; the largest one reported was about 8 cm long. In general appearance and behaviour it can best be compared with the emperor tetras (Nematobrycon).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
